{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the leaders brought the shoham stones.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Sifrei Naso 72) that because they were lax in this donation and did not bring their offering until the end, therefore the letter yod was missing from their name — ״וְהַנְּשִׂאִם״ is written defective, for in truth they should not have waited until the end, for perhaps Israel would give everything needed and they would have no portion in the Mishkan at all. And that the letter yod specifically was missing — we explained above in parashat Terumah (Exodus 25:1) because the Holy One, blessed be He, said ״גְּבַהּ עֵינַיִם וּרְחַב לֵבָב אֹתוֹ לֹא אוּכָל״ (Psalms 101:5), and among the leaders there was undoubtedly a spirit of haughtiness in their saying, by way of boast: Who will fill what we leave lacking? But we will fill whatever the public leaves lacking. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, took from their name the letter yod, for only this letter of the Great Name was engraved in their name (נשיא״ם = נשא + י״וד), and that letter HaShem took from them, as if to say: there is no place for it here." "And we may say further, that since the entire Mishkan was an atonement for the sin of the calf that caused the breaking of the tablets and the holy letters flew off — and it is known that the letters possess greater holiness than the tablets themselves — therefore all the people brought to the donation thirteen things mentioned in parashat Terumah, to atone for having caused the flying off of the letters of the tablets, which are expounded through the thirteen hermeneutical measures by which the Torah is expounded; and the leaders were unable to bring any further donation that related to the writing of the tablets, which is the essence, and they were required to bring two shoham stones as atonement for the breaking of the two tablets of stone, and this atonement is not considered equal to the atonement of the people. Therefore the letter yod was missing from their name, for they had no portion in that atonement that came upon the writing of the Ten Commandments — that is, the letters that flew off." "And our Sages of blessed memory (Yoma 75a) expounded ״וְהַנְּשִׂיאִים הֵבִיאוּ״ from the root meaning clouds, as in ״נְשִׂיאִים וְרוּחַ״ etc. (Proverbs 25:14), and they said that the clouds brought the shoham stones. And it appears to me, following what our Sages of blessed memory said (Ta'anit 8b): the rains are withheld only on account of those who pledge charity in public and do not give, as it says ״נְשִׂיאִים וְרוּחַ וְגֶשֶׁם אָיִן אִישׁ מִתְהַלֵּל בְּמַתַּת שָׁקֶר״ — and if so, in a place where the donation is not given, the clouds (נשיאים) bring down nothing at all; but here, where each person gave his donation, therefore it says ״וְהַנְּשִׂיאִים הֵבִיאוּ״ etc., for the clouds gave their rain in their proper time and blessing was sent forth into all the work of their hands, until they were able to acquire shoham stones and every precious stone by virtue of the abundance of wealth that the clouds bestowed upon them. Or that the clouds would draw the waters from the floor of the sea, the place where shoham stones are found." "And by way of allusion one may explain what they said in the Masorah, that ״וַיִּכָּלֵא״ appears twice: first, ״וַיִּכָּלֵא הַגֶּשֶׁם מִן הַשָּׁמָיִם״ (Genesis 8:2); second, ״וַיִּכָּלֵא הָעָם מֵהָבִיא״ (Exodus 36:6) — an allusion that at the time when they do not give their donation and the people are restrained from bringing what they had pledged, then ״וַיִּכָּלֵא הַגֶּשֶׁם מִן הַשָּׁמָיִם״ — the rain is restrained from the heavens. And some say that because the leaders were supplied with the manna and their provisions were readied for them and they had no expenses whatsoever, from there they became rich, for their wealth was constantly increasing and they had in hand enough to purchase shoham stones."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:41.186769317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}